gpu recovery: on bare metal always a full reset, as later Linux does

Linux 6.6's amdgpu_device_pre_asic_reset first tries the IP blocks'
soft resets (check_soft_reset), and without a hung block found it
resumes without resetting the ASIC.  On GFX 11 neither works: gfx's soft
reset resets MES too, which then answers nothing ("MES failed to
response msg=14"), and the reset left the GPU half done (clock and
power gating off: 110 W at idle); without it, the IB tests after the
attempt fail, amdgpu_ib_ring_tests marks the device dead
(accel_working = false: every CS -EBUSY) and the full reset that
follows never revives it.  Later Linux (7.3.1) sets need_full_reset on
bare metal and has no soft reset path there; so here.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c	2026-11-02 09:33:55.722885524 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c	2026-11-02 09:33:55.723207820 +0100
@@ -4753,20 +4753,7 @@
 
 	/* Don't suspend on bare metal if we are not going to HW reset the ASIC */
 	if (!amdgpu_sriov_vf(adev)) {
-
-		if (!need_full_reset)
-			need_full_reset = amdgpu_device_ip_need_full_reset(adev);
-
-		if (!need_full_reset && amdgpu_gpu_recovery &&
-		    amdgpu_device_ip_check_soft_reset(adev)) {
-			amdgpu_device_ip_pre_soft_reset(adev);
-			r = amdgpu_device_ip_soft_reset(adev);
-			amdgpu_device_ip_post_soft_reset(adev);
-			if (r || amdgpu_device_ip_check_soft_reset(adev)) {
-				dev_info(adev->dev, "soft reset failed, will fallback to full reset!\n");
-				need_full_reset = true;
-			}
-		}
+		need_full_reset = true;
 
 		if (need_full_reset)
 			r = amdgpu_device_ip_suspend(adev);
